      "explanation": "The helper switches on \"ABC\".charAt(1), which is always 'B', and that arm assigns a constant; the arms that assign the request value never run. The engine does not evaluate the switch subject, so it keeps every arm and the line-level concatenation match stands. Engine gap; most of the remaining BenchmarkJava SQL false positives are constant-folding tricks of this kind (constant switches and if-conditions, fixed list and map positions)."
